course: dictionary
lesson: 11756
title: Banned: not allowed by the rules
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Banned comes from the verb ban, which means to say officially that something is not allowed. Banned is its past form, so «The club banned phones in lessons» means the club made a rule against phones.
explain: Check the words around it. «Dogs banned» on a park gate tells you that dogs are not allowed in. If you swap in not allowed and the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Banned can also describe a thing. A banned item is one that the rules forbid. «Liquids are banned in the sports hall» is not a matter of opinion; it is a rule. Phrases like banned from, banned items and banned list are common in school and safety rules, so spot them.
fact: Banned means officially not allowed.
fact: Banned is the past form of the verb ban: ban, banned, banned.
fact: «The school banned football at break.» Here banned is a verb.
fact: «The banned items were left at the airport.» Here banned describes the items, so it works like an adjective.
fact: Phrases you may see: banned from, banned items, banned list.
exercise: «Swimming is banned in the lake after the storm.» What does banned mean here? | Open to everyone | Full of fish | *Officially not allowed | Very cold and wet
exercise: A park sign says «Dogs banned». What does the sign tell you? | Dogs are welcome and free to run | Dogs need a lead only | Dogs must be fed here | *Dogs are not allowed in
exercise: Find the word in «The club banned mobile phones during lessons» that is the past form of ban. | lessons | club | *banned | mobile
test: «The airport staff found banned items in her bag.» What are the banned items? | *Items that the rules forbid, so they must not be taken on board | Items for sale at the shop | Items the rules do not allow | Items that are very heavy
test: Ali says banned means a bit damp. Which answer is correct? | Banned means a kind of food | *Banned means officially not allowed | Banned means happy and loud | Banned means damp and cold
exam: Mia reads «Glass bottles banned from the pool.» What does this tell her? | Glass bottles are a good gift for the pool | The pool is closed for the summer | *Glass bottles are not allowed in the pool | Glass bottles are cheap at the pool shop
